          <profiles>
            <profile name="Start of Activation" id="f3aa-43dd-7d04-f836" hidden="false" typeId="d2bb-86b4-edf3-c4e5" typeName="Special Card">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="b4b7-5338-e8e2-41fd">At the start of this model&apos;s activation choose one of the following:
- This model gains Agile until the end of the activation.
- Enemy models within 2&quot; of this model turn to directly face this model.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Gossip" id="3762-cf62-e671-ecd1" hidden="false" typeId="d2bb-86b4-edf3-c4e5" typeName="Special Card">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="b4b7-5338-e8e2-41fd">You may choose one Enemy model before deployment.
Unless that model must be the VIM (because it is the only valid option or due to a Unique Effect), your opponent cannot choose that model to be VIM.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile name="Disguised" id="81d1-cdf6-78be-04ae" hidden="false" typeId="2f00-4eb0-a8cb-7022" typeName="Unique Effects">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="6de4-d067-c2aa-0dc2">While this model has a Disguised Marker, enemy models with a Ki Statistic of 2 or less cannot Target or voluntarily move into BtB with the Disguised model.
When this model loses its Disguised Marker after declaring a Melee or Ranged Action, its Targets are Surprised until the current action is resolved.
While this model has a Disguised Marker, it loses the Camouflage trait and enemy models in an Opposed Ki test with this model are Surprised, regardless of the usual
requirements.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
        </infoGroup>
